                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "c9a0929b-6313-4e68-aa43-a93ba473e205",
                        "entry_id": "c77360b5-9716-3b6a-aee5-d1bbaab112ae",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mewses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b90bfcad-5ece-3e82-9861-285c5836accc",
                        "entry_id": "c77360b5-9716-3b6a-aee5-d1bbaab112ae",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An alley where there are stables; a narrow passage; a confined place."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1740a03c-1487-4d18-b006-e51410aa858b",
                                "sense_id": "b90bfcad-5ece-3e82-9861-285c5836accc",
                                "text": "What penned them there, with all the plain to choose?\n No foot-print leading to that horrid mews,\n None out of it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f20019be-72a9-41aa-90ae-82598bf94ef7",
                                "sense_id": "b90bfcad-5ece-3e82-9861-285c5836accc",
                                "text": "It was healthy and magnificient because one room, above a mews, somewhere near the river, contained fifty excited, talkative, friendly people."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "383ae8fd-b675-406e-8ae4-d5238755d50e",
                                "sense_id": "b90bfcad-5ece-3e82-9861-285c5836accc",
                                "text": "It was here in the kitchen, in the passage\nIn the mews in the harn in the byre in the market place[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ac48447-bd21-4384-90b9-ec712a4de5c7",
                                "sense_id": "b90bfcad-5ece-3e82-9861-285c5836accc",
                                "text": "It was further proposed that a space of ground near these establishments should be appropriated to a mews for the convenience of persons requiring post horses, and for the standing of horses and carriages at livery."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5de5fc46-baa7-4a9d-9884-b0ff533c9683",
                                "sense_id": "b90bfcad-5ece-3e82-9861-285c5836accc",
                                "text": "[Pavilion Road is] a cobbled mews lined with butchers, cheesemongers, florists and cafés offering a village-like counterpoint to the grandeur of the main thoroughfare."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
